VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...

# The relay's base URL. Local development points at the relay running on your own machine;
# a deployed build must point at the deployed relay over https, e.g.
#   VITE_RELAY_HTTP_URL=https://companion-relay.onrender.com
#
# These are baked in at BUILD time by Vite, not read at runtime — changing them on the host
# requires a rebuild/redeploy, not just a restart.
VITE_RELAY_HTTP_URL=http://localhost:8787

# Optional. The WebSocket URL is derived from VITE_RELAY_HTTP_URL automatically (https -> wss),
# so you normally leave this unset. Set it only if the WebSocket lives somewhere other than the
# HTTP origin. See packages/web/src/config.ts for why deriving it is the default: a deploy that
# set only the HTTP URL used to leave the socket on ws://localhost, which an https page blocks as
# mixed content — presenting as an app stuck on "reconnecting…" forever with nothing in the UI
# explaining why.
# VITE_RELAY_WS_URL=
